<urn:usf:acceptance:hermes-feedback> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require a stable observation identity, UTC observation timestamp, source identity, clock-instance identity, monotonic phase offsets, and explicit nullable joins for attempt, logical attempt, issue, lane, work, realisation basis digest, route, validation, merge and comparable scope. The helper never infers a missing join from CWD, process, provider output, Git, ledger or history. A supplied settled result reference carries immutable identity/digest, verification state, settled attempt, comparable scope and semantic disposition. The helper validates exact join equality but cannot authenticate the reference. Accepted-progress or ROI guidance requires independently-verified-by-consuming-runtime, accepted disposition and exact accepted join. Missing, unverified, stale, cross-scope, unsettled or mismatching references refuse that claim. Compute only monotonic observed phase-wall duration from supplied non-negative offsets in one declared clock instance/domain. It is not queue time, model-active time, CPU time, provider latency, total elapsed time or accepted-progress duration. Queue/model-active durations and input/output tokens are either known nonnegative values with explicit producer provenance or null with null provenance; never synthesize them from UTC, lifecycle records or historical summaries. Raw provider outcome is distinct from semantic disposition. Accepted-progress or ROI advisory guidance requires at least three distinct settled accepted attempt identities with independently verified result references, one comparable scope and one measurement definition. Separately, recurring-failure advisory guidance requires at least three distinct settled attempt identities with one comparable scope and one eligible failure disposition: failed-validation, provider-failure or merge-failure. Retry lineage cannot count as distinct attempts. A failure proposal never claims accepted progress or ROI. Either proposal is advisory data only and cannot activate semantics, alter routing, update a host skill or apply itself. Require each guidance context item to be explicitly allowlisted, digest-addressed and provenance-identified, with attributed source name/digest and import version. The USF operator guidance adaptation is repository content only, not a runtime dependency on a Codex host path, session or private skill installation. Reject unknown, duplicate, private, ambient, undigested, digest-mismatched or non-allowlisted context. Private Codex runtime state, credentials, chat/session material, host paths, provider-specific prompts and unbounded repository content are forbidden. Completion validation exercises accepted and recurring-failure joins, explicit nullable durable joins, unverified/stale/mismatched references, raw-outcome versus semantic-disposition separation, monotonic ordering and safe arithmetic, provenance-required reported queue/model-active/tokens, scope/disposition comparability, duplicate and fewer-than-three attempts, context allowlist/digest/provenance refusal, deterministic output and absence of side effects. It does not establish construction authority and does not access a live ledger, site, provider, host skill or private Codex runtime." <urn:usf:graph:hermes-feedback> .
