<urn:usf:requirement:hermes-feedback-repeated-evidence> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Accepted-progress or ROI advisory guidance requires at least three distinct settled accepted attempt identities with independently verified result references, one comparable scope and one measurement definition. Separately, recurring-failure advisory guidance requires at least three distinct settled attempt identities with one comparable scope and one eligible failure disposition: failed-validation, provider-failure or merge-failure. Retry lineage cannot count as distinct attempts. A failure proposal never claims accepted progress or ROI. Either proposal is advisory data only and cannot activate semantics, alter routing, update a host skill or apply itself." <urn:usf:graph:hermes-feedback> .
